The concept and the name "instinct" (an atomic learned behaviour an agent
carries, with a confidence score) come from ECC (formerly named everything-claude-code),
https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC, skills/continuous-learning-v2, distributed
under the MIT License. No ECC source code is included in this project: ECC's
instincts are natural-language triggers, while the matcher, delivery policy,
activation log and measurement tools here were written for this project.

The rules in examples/instincts/ are synthetic, written for the demo and the
tests. None of them records anyone's real history.
